<section class="mb-5">
  <div class="card shadow-sm border-0">
    <div class="card-body p-4 p-lg-5">
      <h2 class="h1 mb-3">Sand Point Way can be better</h2>
      <p class="lead">
        Sand Point Way NE runs through northeast Seattle, connecting the University
        District to Magnuson Park and beyond. For decades it served as State Route
        513 &mdash; a designation that prioritised cars over everyone else.
      </p>
      <p class="mb-4">
        The highway designation is gone, but the road culture has not caught up.
        <strong>Beyond SR 513</strong> is a community advocacy effort pushing for
        safer crossings, protected bike lanes, and pedestrian-friendly streetscaping
        along Sand Point Way NE.
      </p>
      <div class="d-flex flex-wrap gap-2">
        <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/get-involved/">Get involved</a>
        <a class="btn btn-outline-primary" href="/about/">Learn more</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="row g-4 mb-5">
  <div class="col-md-6">
    <div class="card h-100 shadow-sm">
      <div class="card-body">
        <h2 class="h4 card-title">The problem</h2>
        <p class="card-text mb-0">
          Sand Point Way NE has long stretches with no safe crossing, narrow or
          non-existent sidewalks, and fast-moving traffic that makes walking or
          cycling feel dangerous. Nearby destinations &mdash; Magnuson Park,
          Children&rsquo;s Hospital, the Burke-Gilman Trail, and residential
          neighbourhoods &mdash; deserve better connections.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="col-md-6">
    <div class="card h-100 shadow-sm">
      <div class="card-body">
        <h2 class="h4 card-title">Why now</h2>
        <p class="card-text mb-0">
          We believe a road that once moved state highway traffic can be redesigned
          to move people &mdash; on foot, on bikes, and in transit &mdash; while
          remaining a useful corridor for cars.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="mb-5">
  <h2 class="h3 mb-3">Our vision</h2>
  <div class="list-group shadow-sm">
    <div class="list-group-item">Protected pedestrian crossings at every major intersection</div>
    <div class="list-group-item">Continuous sidewalks on both sides of the road</div>
    <div class="list-group-item">A protected bike lane connecting the Burke-Gilman Trail to Magnuson Park</div>
    <div class="list-group-item">Street trees and traffic calming to reduce vehicle speeds</div>
    <div class="list-group-item">Better bus stops and shelters for Metro Route 75</div>
  </div>
</section>

